{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen","id":1473626,"title":"Rite of the Shrouded Glen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-01-30T19:35:03-08:00","id":1473626,"title":"Rite of the Shrouded Glen","content":"So this level 4 rite renders the interior of a bawn permanently invisible if 10 gnosis is spent upon the casting... but what exactly is the benefit? I can see how it could be useful to prevent scrying, but beyond that...?<br /> <br /> So, a couple of questions:<ul><li>What does invisible mean, exactly? If somebody scries, do they see nothingness, indicating something is hidden? A penumbral reflection of what the land would look like without the caern being there? Or...?</li> <li>Does the rite prevent people walking up to the bawn from seeing what lies inside?</li> <li>Is the Sept invisible to just creatures of the wyrm, or anybody that's not part of the sept, or..?</li> <li>Other then the Rite of Luna's Eye and the Uktena gift of scrying, what other scrying abilities/gifts are there that this gift would foil?</li> </ul>Sorry if these questions are obtuse. Just excited about the rite, but a little confused about the particulars. Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T22:36:36-08:00","id":1473631,"title":"","content":"This is a good question. Our minds think alike. I think one reason I respond to your posts is that often I had to figure these things out in my own chronicles merely 6-12 months before you ask them for yours.<br /> <br /> Obviously the Rite somehow protects the caern by preventing enemies from easily figuring out there is a caern there to raid or invade. After all, we know Mages, marauding spirits, and BSDs would want to despoil them. But first they would have to find them. But to your point, what does that mean in practical terms?<br /> <br /> The mere existence of this caern rite logically implies that a caern is easier to find or detect without this rite being performed. So what should that look like? Well, we're not given descriptions to that effect as far as I can tell. But I can think of some things that might be noteworthy.<br /> <br /> First, caerns often have large concentrations of Garou or other Changing Breeds during their moots. &quot;Hey, it's the night of the full moon, and I can see there's a crap load of Garou over there. Must be a caern there.&quot;<br /> <br /> Second, Garou often open Moon Bridges in the Umbra. A huge moon bridge popping up would be an obvious sign a caern is present. It's like how if you hear jet engines taking off, you're probably near an airport.<br /> <br /> Third, caerns are homes to a lot of spirits besides the caern totem. The spiritual energies of a caern often awaken or attract Gaian spirits. Congregations of large number of spirits is usually because there's either a domain present or a caern is present. So seeing lots of spirits might be a sign that a caern is present.<br /> <br /> Fourth, a caern's penumbra is supposed to be much more integreated with the physical world than elsewhere. It does not mean an exact relationship, but it should at least be identifiable as to where it is. Even things that aren't physically the same, should be spiritually reflections of such (such as the Grave of Hallowed Heroes being obvious as to what it is). Someone who knows the physical world's layout and has some knowledge of caerns, should be able to identify a caern.<br /> <br /> Fifth, we have the caern heart. The caern heart is always identifiable as self-contained area, easily seen as what lies within it and outside it. And inside the caern hear, the physical realm and spiritual world is one and the same. In Garou septs, this is almost always guarded by at least one character like the Warder. So again, this is easily identifiable if one knows what one is looking for.<br /> <br /> There may be more things that this, but currently this is what I can think of.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I reason the Rite of the Shrouded Glen must eliminate these tell tale signs. By making an area of the Umbra invisible (and since this is a caern rite, I assume it can only be done at a caern) it creates a &quot;bubble&quot; where if you are outside it, you can't see these things. Instead, you only see what would normally exist without a caern (Garou and other people are invisible, spirits can't be seen, moon bridges don't appear, none of the distinctive tell tale signs of a caern show, etc.). You only see what the penumbra would be like as if the caern did not exist. Only if you enter the &quot;bubble&quot;, would these things appear. And of course, since everything inside the bubble can see outside of it, they (Garou, the caern totem, allied spirits, whatever) can take action if they see something approaching that shouldn't. They can arrange interceptions, deceptions, ambushes, etc. as needed.<br /> <br /> The Rite of the Shrouded Glen therefore works best against foes who don't already know that there is a caern there. You have strategic surprise in your favor. It's less effective when your enemy already knows there is a caern there from prior knowledge, but even then it still provides tactical surprise for the sept's Garou. If the bad guys approach a caern, they still can't see inside the bubble until they reach it. They have no idea if the sept is unwary, or if they are completely armed and ready for them. They may not know the strongpoints and defenses established internally. All they would know is a vague notion that somewhere in this vicinity there's a caern.<br /> <br /> To some of your questions, if the Rite completely made the area completely blank/invisible, it would defeat the purpose of the Rite. &quot;Hey, there's just a blank white space there, so it must be a caern.&quot; It'd be self-defeating because more often than not, you're drawing more attention to yourself, not less. A level four Rite should be very useful. It should be a cornerstone of any sept's defenses.<br /> <br /> To a certain degree, I think it's similar to how the land of Elfwood is &quot;invisible&quot; in Disenchantment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=L_pj9fI7QAM\" data-code=\"L_pj9fI7QAM\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/L_pj9fI7QAM/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> That's how I'm running it right now. Open to change based on interesting ideas and advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3046,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","user":"Black Fox","date":". 01-31-2022, 01:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T12:19:58-08:00","id":1473687,"title":"","content":"This all accords with what I suspected. Thank you for the clarification, and cue my continued appreciation for your generosity. Often I'm left writing succinct thanks that don't do justice to the amount of information you've shared, but going through each of your points and expressing agreement would be at best redundant, and at worst a simple waste of your time. So: thank you!<br /> <br /> Since we're on this topic, however, how about a follow-up question? <br /> <br /> The scenario is as follows: a level 2 caern dedicated to Owl on Belle Isle in Detroit has just been taken over by an Athro Glasswalker Ahroun, who successfully wrested leadership away from the founder, a Shadow Lord Adren Ahroun. The caern is the sole outpost of Garou activity in all of Detroit, which, being set in the World of Darkness version of 2003, is deeply inimical to their kind. <br /> <br /> The Athro is going to call in favors to have the Rite of the Shrouded Glen cast, but seeing as the large BSD presence in town is already aware of the sept's location, what else could you see a new Grand Elder implementing in terms of security measures? She's mercurial, volatile, violent, and inordinately dangerous in personal combat, but not the most patient or thorough of individuals, and is lacking in personal connections due to her past. I'd like her to flex some higher level know-how, however, along the lines of the level 4 Rite. <br /> <br /> In-game, I've had the BSD's ignore the caern until now due to their being pre-occupied with their own business (cue long term machinations to summon an Incarna of the Wyrm) but they number around 50 or so in Detroit (multiple hives) and could steamroll the caern if it ever properly caught their attention. <br /> <br /> I know the devil's in the details, and that any suggestions you might make will be hamstrung by your lack of knowing the nuances of the game, but low hanging fruit like Shrouded Glen are the kind of things I'd appreciate your pointing out. <br /> <br /> Cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T13:54:02-08:00","id":1473693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The mere existence of this caern rite logically implies that a caern is easier to find or detect without this rite being performed. So what should that look like? Well, we're not given descriptions to that effect as far as I can tell. But I can think of some things that might be noteworthy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fluff indicates that being at a caern can be felt by Garou. It is mentioned that even humans might feel something special about a caern.<br /> <br /> But, you are correct, there is no mechanic I know of either. Within WtA, at least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First, caerns often have large concentrations of Garou or other Changing Breeds during their moots. &quot;Hey, it's the night of the full moon, and I can see there's a crap load of Garou over there. Must be a caern there.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Within reason. Garou and other Changing Breeds might be careful to access the Caern more or less covertly, depending on circumstances. Also, a Bawn has a rough size estimate in 'Guardians of the Caerns', iirc, and not all sites a typical caern has need to be in close proximity. The gathering area, guest quarters and Heart of the Caern can be relatively far away from each other.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, Garou often open Moon Bridges in the Umbra. A huge moon bridge popping up would be an obvious sign a caern is present. It's like how if you hear jet engines taking off, you're probably near an airport.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is something that the way I understand the description, would not happen. The Moon Bridge at a Caern is a direct portal into the Atherial Realm, where the bridge spans from one portal to another, which then leads back into the material world, usually. The Bridges do not necessarily lead through the Penumbra and can't necessarily be spotted as appearing and disappearing, if one isn't inside the Atherial Realm itself (there they can be seen, as per description of the Realm, iirc).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, caerns are homes to a lot of spirits besides the caern totem. The spiritual energies of a caern often awaken or attract Gaian spirits. Congregations of large number of spirits is usually because there's either a domain present or a caern is present. So seeing lots of spirits might be a sign that a caern is present.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. If one would systematically go through the Penumbra and try to find higher concentrations of spirits in general, or more jagglings as opposed to gaffelings, then one might be finding a caern. On the other hand, talking to spirits, might yield the same effect. Spirits might not describe a Caern accurately, but can still give indicators as to where caerns might be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fourth, a caern's penumbra is supposed to be much more integrated with the physical world than elsewhere. It does not mean an exact relationship, but it should at least be identifiable as to where it is. Even things that aren't physically the same, should be spiritually reflections of such (such as the Grave of Hallowed Heroes being obvious as to what it is). Someone who knows the physical world's layout and has some knowledge of caerns, should be able to identify a caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>True.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fifth, we have the caern heart. The caern heart is always identifiable as self-contained area, easily seen as what lies within it and outside it. And inside the caern hear, the physical realm and spiritual world is one and the same. In Garou septs, this is almost always guarded by at least one character like the Warder. So again, this is easily identifiable if one knows what one is looking for.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure as to the easiness to spot or the obviousness of discerning the caern heart, but sure, a person with some experience might recognise it. Then again, it is guarded and a stranger shouldn't come near it, hopefully.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, I reason the Rite of the Shrouded Glen must eliminate these tell tale signs. By making an area of the Umbra invisible (and since this is a caern rite, I assume it can only be done at a caern) it creates a &quot;bubble&quot; where if you are outside it, you can't see these things. Instead, you only see what would normally exist without a caern (Garou and other people are invisible, spirits can't be seen, moon bridges don't appear, none of the distinctive tell tale signs of a caern show, etc.). You only see what the penumbra would be like as if the caern did not exist. Only if you enter the &quot;bubble&quot;, would these things appear. And of course, since everything inside the bubble can see outside of it, they (Garou, the caern totem, allied spirits, whatever) can take action if they see something approaching that shouldn't. They can arrange interceptions, deceptions, ambushes, etc. as needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I understood the Rite, the caern doesn't necessarily change in the physical world, visibly. In the Penumbra, Fog shrouds the site, once you are on the same scene as the carn bawn perimeter. From further away, the area should look unsuspicious (no dome of fog, that would reveal something is hidden there). In any case, light, perception, distance are all not adhering to the laws of physics in the Penumbra, so....<br /> <br /> Besides that, attempts at scrying are blocked (as in, fail, if tried), and this works for the caern itself, as well as all persons or objects inside the Rite, in the physical world or the penumbra. Within the shrouded are, the garou can side step normally, and leave the shrouded area without problem, but attempts at entering lead to them being lost in the fog.<br /> Moon Bridges established via Pathstone would still work, but while the Shrouding is in effect no new or temporary Moon Bridges can target the shrouded are, meaning the Rite of Lunas Spear, the Bridge Walker Gift or the Moon Bridge spirit Charm would fail. Open Moon Bridge would work, if there was a Moon Bridge to begin with.<br /> <br /> I'd extend this protections to other magical means by other supernatural beings, like blocking Auspex 7, for example, or Correspondence effects, Hedge Magic and so on...<br /> <br /> One drawback is, that spirits send as messengers can't reach the caerns or garou there, either. That is, unless the garou leave the caern area for their pack territories...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473631#post1473631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite of the Shrouded Glen therefore works best against foes who don't already know that there is a caern there. You have strategic surprise in your favor. It's less effective when your enemy already knows there is a caern there from prior knowledge, but even then it still provides tactical surprise for the sept's Garou. If the bad guys approach a caern, they still can't see inside the bubble until they reach it. They have no idea if the sept is unwary, or if they are completely armed and ready for them. They may not know the strongpoints and defenses established internally. All they would know is a vague notion that somewhere in this vicinity there's a caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>It can also be an additional protection, of you prepare for an attack and suspect your enemy has scrying capabilities. Or an attack is underway, and you want the few who remained to protect the caern to not have to worry about attackers through the penumbra.<br /> <br /> That is how I run it....<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T14:02:37-08:00","id":1473695,"title":"","content":"As for what a Glasswalker would to to increase security?<br /> Well, Glasswalker might not have to much problem to have outposts on the shore lines (of the island and on the main land) watch all maritime traffic as an early warning system. Generally, I think garou should shy away from technology, but Glasswalkers are Glasswakers after all. So, there are probably cameras and computer analysis to help with such affairs, not just kinfolk/garou with binoculars.<br /> Spirits can be bound into services other than Talens with the Rite of Binding. Especially Owl as caern spirit would probably help to attract some winged predators who can perfectly provide early warning capabilities for the Penumbra. There are also Skulls of killed enemies that can act as warning sirens if put on a stick. Not sure if it was a Rite, Talen or Fetish, and probably not a good idea, if human park rangers or someone like that would spot those.<br /> There is a BoneGnawer, no tresspassing Rite, that might also work well, especially if paired with actual no trespassing signs by local authorities. They wouldn't bother BSD, but they will keep most humans at bay and reduce alarms given by meaningless intruders.<br /> <br /> Even Glasswalkers should, in my opinion, shy away from stuff like mines or auto turrets.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T15:01:05-08:00","id":1473701,"title":"","content":"Heinrich, thanks for your comments. It's always interesting to hear your take because your long standing LARP has wrestled with a lot of these same issues.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473693#post1473693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fluff indicates that being at a caern can be felt by Garou. It is mentioned that even humans might feel something special about a caern.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense. It may be unimportant though as I don't think that's the kind of thing that can be turned invisible, but it's certainly noteworthy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473693#post1473693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is something that the way I understand the description, would not happen. The Moon Bridge at a Caern is a direct portal into the Atherial Realm, where the bridge spans from one portal to another, which then leads back into the material world, usually. The Bridges do not necessarily lead through the Penumbra and can't necessarily be spotted as appearing and disappearing, if one isn't inside the Atherial Realm itself (there they can be seen, as per description of the Realm, iirc).</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right that the arch itself leads into the Atherial Realm and therefore is one of those things that should vanish into the non-three dimensional parts of the Umbra. However, the opening and closing of the &quot;gate&quot; of the Moon Bridge should be seen in the Penumbra itself if the Moon Bridge is opened in the Penumbra as opposed to the physical realm. Because prying eyes might always see something in the physical realm, I usually see most STs and players choose to open the Moon Bridge in the Penumbra (or some very secluded location in the physical realm). And it's that &quot;gate&quot; I imagine would be often quite noticeable from a distance since it's made out of a Lune and therefore moonlight. I should have been more clear.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473693#post1473693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I understood the Rite, the caern doesn't necessarily change in the physical world, visibly. In the Penumbra, Fog shrouds the site, once you are on the same scene as the carn bawn perimeter. From further away, the area should look unsuspicious (no dome of fog, that would reveal something is hidden there). In any case, light, perception, distance are all not adhering to the laws of physics in the Penumbra, so....</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the first time I've seen this be portrayed as a fog enshrouding the site, as opposed to rendering things invisible. Yes, the rite itself is called &quot;shrouded&quot; glen, but the actual description clearly states &quot;invisible.&quot; Do you know of any actual reference where anything like a dome of fog is mentioned? I wonder if that may be something either you or your LARP group determined differently from what's in the actual text. I just checked some older corebooks to see if the rite description ever changed (this happens sometimes), but even in second edition core, the rite clearly states it causes an area to become invisible, not covered in fog. Maybe I'm not understanding what you mean because later you state people don't see a dome of fog.<br /> <br /> But yes, the caern in the physical world shouldn't be impacted at all. It's only how things look in the Penumbra.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473693#post1473693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Moon Bridges established via Pathstone would still work, but while the Shrouding is in effect no new or temporary Moon Bridges can target the shrouded are, meaning the Rite of Lunas Spear, the Bridge Walker Gift or the Moon Bridge spirit Charm would fail. Open Moon Bridge would work, if there was a Moon Bridge to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's definitely going beyond the description of the Rite. It doesn't say anything about affecting Moon Bridges. If the people using those Gifts/Rites are at the caern, they should work as normal. And if the people are away, but know of the caern's existence, then why shouldn't they still work even if it's invisible from outside the area? I think this is clearly an alternate House Rule as opposed to something that can be derived from the rite description itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-31T15:47:20-08:00","id":1473703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473687#post1473687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Athro is going to call in favors to have the Rite of the Shrouded Glen cast, but seeing as the large BSD presence in town is already aware of the sept's location, what else could you see a new Grand Elder implementing in terms of security measures?</div> </div> </div> </div>Who you pick as the Warder and Guardians will be important since those will likely be the only Garou on hand when the BSDs attack. Since they could very well die defending the caern, you want experienced Garou, but not the people you want to be future leaders who will need to survive.<br /> <br /> You may also want some kind of actual defensive structure they can retreat too on the caern heart (if possible) so they can prolong the combat as long as possible. Something that prevents the BSDs from using their numbers to their advantage, and which would allow wounded Garou to retreat and heal up before going back to the frontline.<br /> <br /> Other than that, there are some Fetishes that should always be useful.<br /> <br /> Sanctuary Chimes will prevent any unfriendly spirits materializing.<br /> <br /> Guardians of the Caerns has several fetishes designed for sept defense. One is the Sentry's Voice, which is a horn that only the sept members can hear. Another is the Watchspear that warns of Wyrm creatures in the Umbra when they approach within 200 yards.<br /> <br /> But you don't want to leave behind Fetishes that can't be allowed to fall into enemy hands. You don't want the sept's only Klaive to be there. You want it in someone else's hand who can escape.<br /> <br /> It's also good to have certain Talens stockpiled before hand they can be used extensively like Bane Arrows, Gaia's Breath, Nightshade, and Wyrm Sign. That'll be good for the Garou stuck in their little fortress trying to fend off 50 BSDs.<br /> <br /> You will also want good scouts that can patrol the Bawn or even spy on the known locations of BSDs. That might mean use of talens like Chiopteran Spies. Local spirits already living on the Bawn. Spirits you bound into service or have given chiminage too who. That may notify you in advance of an attack so which might put enough people on alert that the counterattack can be quicker. Likewise, some of these spirits could be used for actual combat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473687#post1473687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In-game, I've had the BSD's ignore the caern until now due to their being pre-occupied with their own business (cue long term machinations to summon an Incarna of the Wyrm) but they number around 50 or so in Detroit (multiple hives) and could steamroll the caern if it ever properly caught their attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that large a number of BSDs would certainly overrun a caern. That being the case, it would behoove the sept to have planned for it to fall initially given the number of Garou they have at their disposal. Instead of sacrificing everything in a futile defense (although some guardians would need to sacrifice themselves on principle to maintain the sept's honor and to defend the caern totem), what the sept needs to do is have organized a counterattack with reinforcements to occur in a time period before the BSDs can corrupt the caern. In other words, have the army fall back into the Bataan Peninsula and activate War Plan Orange (note, this actually didn't turn out well for MacArthur in the Philippines so even good plans can fail).<br /> <br /> That means the Gatekeeper (the sept's diplomat) sending out her Moonwalkers and making alliances with those septs willing to commit to this caern's defense and send overwhelming numbers of Garou to take back the sept. Given every sept wants to ensure their sept is defended first and the population decline of Garou, this isn't necessarily easy. But in Under a Blood Red Moon, the fall of the Fanum caused a large number of Garou to assemble to take it back. So ultimately I think &quot;delay the enemy, and wait for reinforcements&quot; will need to be the primary defensive strategy. <br /> <br /> That means lots of preparations. Work on establishing those alliances, and have certain packs stay behind to harry the BSDs in a guerilla war and collect intelligence that will be useful when the counterattack occurs. For example, rather than have the sept's packs who aren't Guardians come rushing into the caern, where they might be slaughtered, they may want to have a predetermined assembly point, and someone who can perform the rite of the Badger's Burrow who can ask questions like &quot;Has the caern fallen yet?&quot;, &quot;How many Black Spiral Dancers are attacking?&quot;, &quot;What other Wyrm creatures are with them?&quot; and the like. Given Garou's Rage and culture, this might be easier said than done, so it's important good leaders are selected who can command the others, and they follow a flexible, but prepared plan. <br /> <br /> As General Eisenhower said, plans are useless, but planning is indispensable. The sept's members should have a clear idea on the general strategy and what they need to do when the attack comes. But be prepared to be flexible since they can't predict what the BSDs will actually do. This is where the importance of having good Adrens and Athros come into play to be the leaders that the cliaths and fosterns need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T01:45:18-08:00","id":1473739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473701#post1473701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are right that the arch itself leads into the Atherial Realm and therefore is one of those things that should vanish into the non-three dimensional parts of the Umbra. However, the opening and closing of the &quot;gate&quot; of the Moon Bridge should be seen in the Penumbra itself if the Moon Bridge is opened in the Penumbra as opposed to the physical realm. Because prying eyes might always see something in the physical realm, I usually see most STs and players choose to open the Moon Bridge in the Penumbra (or some very secluded location in the physical realm). And it's that &quot;gate&quot; I imagine would be often quite noticeable from a distance since it's made out of a Lune and therefore moonlight. I should have been more clear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see what you mean. True, although the Portal might be look the same if the Gift Bridge Walker or the spirit Charm were used. So, yeah, regularly opening Portals might indicate a caern, but also the pack territory of a pack that makes frequent use of other means to open Moon Bridges.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473701#post1473701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is the first time I've seen this be portrayed as a fog enshrouding the site, as opposed to rendering things invisible. Yes, the rite itself is called &quot;shrouded&quot; glen, but the actual description clearly states &quot;invisible.&quot; Do you know of any actual reference where anything like a dome of fog is mentioned? I wonder if that may be something either you or your LARP group determined differently from what's in the actual text. I just checked some older corebooks to see if the rite description ever changed (this happens sometimes), but even in second edition core, the rite clearly states it causes an area to become invisible, not covered in fog. Maybe I'm not understanding what you mean because later you state people don't see a dome of fog.</div> </div> </div> </div>1st Edition mentioned &quot;Those who approach it, in fact, often find themselves walking in circles without ever getting close.&quot; I think that this description, combined with the name of the Rite lead to depicting it like this. The first German version of the Core Rules might also have been a factor, but I don't have the books close, so I can't read how the first translation describes the Rite.<br /> But the Elfwood analogy or some tricking of senses to just ignore the area shrouded works well, too. In any case, it would betray the purpose if there was a blank spot....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473701#post1473701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that's definitely going beyond the description of the Rite. It doesn't say anything about affecting Moon Bridges. If the people using those Gifts/Rites are at the caern, they should work as normal. And if the people are away, but know of the caern's existence, then why shouldn't they still work even if it's invisible from outside the area? I think this is clearly an alternate House Rule as opposed to something that can be derived from the rite description itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, yes, people could reach from the shrouded caern to the outside, but not vice versa, imo. The reasoning behind it possibly was, that it wouldn't be much of a defensive Rite, if it could be circumvented by &quot;teleporting&quot; in. But yeah, it is beyond the scope of what is written in the tabletop.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T07:12:14-08:00","id":1473749,"title":"","content":"I particularly love the idea of planning to fall back so as to swoop in right after and recapture the Sept with overwhelming numbers. Lots of great info here in general, and lots for me to ponder. <br /> <br /> Brilliant.<br /> <br /> Question: how long would it take a bunch of BSD's to corrupt a level 2 sept? Is there a rite they must perform? Is it a gradual process, or something they build up to and then execute?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T07:52:18-08:00","id":1473751,"title":"","content":"You mean a level 2 caern?<br /> There is a mention of a Rite to clean a Pit to get a Carn back, but no system is given beyond the small mention of the name. One could assume the reverse is also possible, but a gradual process is also possible. One could assume that one would fight the caern spirit, and once in slumber completely destroys it. Then, the caern is in danger of dying as well, but a new spirit, like a bane, could tie itself to the caern and corrupt it...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-01T14:12:19-08:00","id":1473775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>pwtucker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1473626-rite-of-the-shrouded-glen?p=1473749#post1473749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: how long would it take a bunch of BSD's to corrupt a level 2 sept? Is there a rite they must perform? Is it a gradual process, or something they build up to and then execute?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only place I know that addresses the issues of corrupting or reclaiming a caern is the second edition Players Guide to Werewolf. That has a lot of information that does not seem to be mentioned anywhere else, but since it is not a Revised product, it often gets overlooked. The relevant pages are on page 110-111. There are probably very few games that actually use these rules. So while I am summarizing them for you, it doesn't mean it's something you must use. But even so, it might be good for inspiration.<br /> <br /> We're told several things. First, the Black Spiral Dancers must perform the Rite of Desceration. The first half of the rite is to bind the caern totem to the physical realm. It may take as long as 36 hours for the first half of the Rite to be performed. The ritemaster must make Manipulation + Rituals rolls (Diff 7). He needs to gather 50 successes on extended rolls while not making more than 18 rolls. If he botches at any time, the rite fails and the caern totem escapes. If the ritemaster is disturbed at any time, the rite fails and he takes 5 aggravated health levels from the angry caern totem. Presumably, if the ritemaster cannot complete the ritual in 18 rolls, the rite also fails and he would take 5 aggravated health levels and the caern totem escapes.<br /> <br /> Simultaneous with the ritemaster making checks, there is a second portion of the Rite. Some other BSD (a chosen champion) must duel the caern totem. Only if this Dancer defeats the totem AND the ritemaster makes all the successes needed, a new Wyrm totem appears and the the defeated caern totem is forced to serve the new Totem.<br /> <br /> THEN the ritemaster must make one final Charisma + Rituals roll (diff 5 + caern level) to transform the caern into a new corrupted caern type. WP cannot be spent. The # of successes is the number of ranks the new Pit has. The new type is some corrupt variant of the old type. If the ritemaster fails in this roll, he may be shunted into Erebus (!) and any other BSD rite participants take five aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> (The next pages after this section then has the way that Gaian Garou can reclaim a corrupted caern, so this is not a one way thing.)<br /> <br /> This provides us a lot of information, but it leads to a lot of questions, and there are aspects of the rite I personally don't like. We're not told the level of the Rite. It seems to be that each roll of the Rite takes two hours to perform, but this is not made explicit. I also presume that should the caern totem escape, then the ritemaster can't perform the final check to corrupt the caern. But again, this is not explicit. What happens if the other BSD defeats the totem, but the ritemaster fails? Can he try again and start anew, or is it over? What happens when the caern totem flees (as caern totems are not supposed to be able to leave the caern), does it mean the caern is rendered inactive, destroyed, something else? (If so, can it be reactivated, or would it need an entire new Rite of Caern Building). What happens to a defeated caern totem serving a Wyrm spirit if the second roll fails? What happens if more than one BSD attempts to fight the caern totem? Presumably that causes the rite to fail. As written, there is no connection between the rank of a Gaian caern and the corrupted caern. You could end up with a Rank 5 Pit in place of a Rank 1 caern. Does that make sense? Maybe you want to limit the corrupted caern rank to be no higher than the level of the former caern.<br /> <br /> There's also another issue. The Rite of Desecration is to corrupt a Gaian caern into a new BSD Pit. They don't need to do this if all they want to do is pollute or ravage the caern so it can no longer function in its purpose. Just ruin its appropriateness for whatever type of caern there is. Presumably the BSDs also have a variant of the Rite of Caern Building to build straight up Wyrm pits instead of corrupting Gaian caerns. But I don't think that's ever mentioned.<br /> <br /> So despite the wealth of information provided in this section, it is also insufficient. An ST wanting to use the 2e Players Guide rules will still need to make a lot of calls.<br /> <br /> So what's the purpose of the BSDs here? It's probably not to just maraud and damage the caern. Belle Isle is in the middle of Detroit, not an isolated part of the wilderness. They just can't truck in toxic waste and dump it. It'd cause too many issues with the humans. If they want to do or some other means of spoiling the caern, they'll likely have to prepare things so they can do it - which should give Garou time to respond assuming they spot these preparations. Presumably, they do want to corrupt the caern.<br /> <br /> But corrupting the caern will take some effort. They will need a chosen champion who can defeat the caern totem in a ritualized combat. And they will need a highly skilled ritemaster who can collect the necessary number of extended successes. If those two Garou participate in the attack, they'll need time to recover. If they are held back until the battle is won, then they could theoretically begin the Rite of Desecration early. But remember the BSDs will need other participants in the rite, and will probably want as many members as they can get to reduce the difficulty. They'll also need other BSDs to protect the rite group. The Ritemaster certainly will not want to start the Rite until he's sure he can do so without interruption as it could easily kill him or ruin the rite (this is one area where ongoing harassment by sept members could be beneficial - it could buy time for others to arrive in force. Even a suicide mission by a small group of Garou could be successful in disrupting the rite for one turn and causing it to fail).<br /> <br /> This could also be used to explain why BSDs don't attack the caern. They don't want to prematurely attack it before they completely their own preparations for the caern. Maybe they are awaiting for a highly skilled Theurge to arrive, or there are disputes among the Hive as to who will be the chosen champion to duel the caern totem, or they need time to arrange a terrible &quot;accident&quot; to occur at Belle Isle shortly after their intended attack and conquest. It's not just a matter of attacking and sept and killing Garou. They need their own plan to accomplish their aims afterwards. If it means taking over the caern, it means being able to defend the new Hive. Maybe they need to build their numbers up even more?<br /> <br /> Rather than running the Rite of Desecration as is, you may want to simplify it for your needs. If you want to make things urgent, limit it to 24 hours before the Garou need to counterattack. Or maybe you want to give the BSDs some time to recover and pacify the area before performing the Rite. That would give outside Garou more time to respond (and this is realistic, it takes time to summon and assemble enough Garou to defeat 50 BSDs). And it would allow a stay behind group (perhaps the PCs) to conduct harassments of the BSDs so they keep delaying performance of the Rite (perhaps even indefinitely). Or you may want to establish a set period of time you think is just right - like 48 or 72 hours or whatever number you like.<br /> <br /> Or go your own way using the things you like as inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T10:41:21-08:00","id":1473839,"title":"","content":"Excellent, thank you. <br /> <br /> I think I'll run with the following:<ul><li>Have the BSD's swarm in, tripping alarms and driving the Garou away into their planned retreat.</li> <li>Give the players and NPC's 24 hours to marshal their response, the strength of which will be determined by the successes of previous diplomatic overtures</li> <li>Splice in mini-BSD narrative scenes where the BSD Theurge runs each step of the Rite of Desecration. I'll not roll die, as this will be more of a story structure element, but doing so I think will both increase the urgency, deepen the poignancy and rage of seeing their home caern and totem attacked, and increase the cinematic tension of deciding how long to spend gathering reinforcements.</li> <li>If the players/good NPC's come up with ways ahead of time/during the retreat to disrupt the Rite, great. If not, it proceeds apace.</li> <li>Run a big revenge battle as the good guys come roaring back to reclaim the sept, probably just before the culmination of the Rite of Desecration. I'll tweak things so that the PC's are the ones who break through and face the BSD Theurge, giving them the appropriate heroic moment to save the caern.</li> </ul>Again, this is all brilliant. Thanks Black Fox and heinrich for your invaluable input.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26645-pwtucker","name":"pwtucker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26645_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]}]